CM_ "CAN FD frames tunnel classic CAN messages as 12-byte chunks: a 4-byte header (16-bit inner id, subid, dlc) then up to 8 data bytes, zero-padded. In chunk 0, data byte 0 (byte 4) = CRC8 poly 0x1D init 0x00 over data bytes 1-7, and data byte 1 (byte 5) low nibble = rolling counter 0-14; the <Message>Checksum/<Message>Counter pairs are that chunk-0 pair.";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKACmd "steering angle setpoint, same scale as StrgWhlAng; frozen at 0 while LKACmdSts is not 4. Offset is -2037.5 (hardware neutral raw 0x7F58), not -2048.";
CM_ SG_ 137 LkaCmdChecksum "CRC8 poly 0x1D init 0x00 over data bytes 5-11.";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKAReqToq "byte 16; not the steering command (LKACmd is the command). Role tentative.";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKACmdPV "14-bit rolling protection value over the LKA command; 0x300 + C when active, 0x400 when idle. Not fully reverse-engineered.";
CM_ BO_ 137 "bytes 16-23 are a second inner message (LKA torque request), protected by LKACmdPV rather than the byte-4 CRC8.";
CM_ SG_ 171 StrgWhlAngRate "reads 0 while the wheel is held steady.";
CM_ SG_ 318 VehSpdAvg "a second speed copy is at bytes 32-33.";
CM_ SG_ 318 DrvrSbltBuckled "complementary to DrvrSbltUnbuckled; both 0 with ignition off.";
CM_ SG_ 319 WhlSpdFR "0.03125 scale, coarser than the other three wheels; left/right verified via turns, front/rear not.";
CM_ SG_ 319 LatAccel "reads -32 m/s2 when invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 474 AccSts "1 = ACC engaged without TJA; 2 = ACC with TJA active.";
CM_ SG_ 474 AccMainOn "ACC main switch / available latch.";
CM_ SG_ 497 BrkHoldActive "brake-hold active; also set for manual braking, not ACC-specific.";
CM_ SG_ 1019 DircnIndSwSts "stalk state without direction; use TURN_SIGNALS for direction.";
CM_ BO_ 80 "bus 1 (radar domain). 16-bit checksum + rolling counters; byte 6 is a slow counter that re-seeds each ignition.";
CM_ BO_ 1808 "GWM/EVCC/BMS addresses from the OBDb MG-MG4 signalset; possibly reachable only via the OBD-II port.";
CM_ BO_ 1842 "ECUs that answered the VIN query (22 F190) on bus 0; FVCM/RADAR naming assumed.";
VAL_ 137 LKACmdSts 0 "OFF" 4 "ACTIVE";
VAL_ 404 ShftLvrPos 1 "P" 2 "R" 4 "D";
VAL_ 474 AccSts 0 "OFF" 1 "ACC_ENGAGED" 2 "ACC_AND_TJA";
VAL_ 1019 DircnIndSwSts 0 "OFF" 1 "TAP" 2 "LATCHED";
